%S A398798 1,2,22,528,24072,2072900,341315998,109061958874,68308578750154,
%T A398798 84341635925162212,205978446112461169878,997127733794623672403416,
%U A398798 9582756798863547123813301372,183035821365687928035629602116772,6954613785672623372205075414476757402
%N A398798 Number of reducible flow graphs on n unlabeled nodes with distinguished entry r and exit t reachable from every node (r = t if n = 1, else r != t), counted up to isomorphism fixing r and t.
%C A398798 Reducible single-entry single-exit control-flow graphs up to entry- and exit-preserving isomorphism, self-loops disallowed.
%C A398798 Computed exactly by the equivariant Burnside recurrence over the permutations fixing entry and exit (see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program of A397968).
%D A398798 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A398798 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A398798 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A398798 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A398798 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A398798 a(n) = (1/(n-2)!) * Sum over cycle types mu of n-2 elements of permcount(mu) * F_R2(mu) for n >= 2, with a(1)=1, where F_R2 is the equivariant SCC-region recurrence augmented by the co-reachability inclusion-exclusion for the fixed exit.
%o A398798 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_cfgs_single_sink", 16) # See Python link in A397968 for program code.
%Y A398798 Cf. A397968 (entry-only version), A345258 (acyclic analog, necessarily all reducible).
%K A398798 nonn,new
%O A398798 1,2
%A A398798 _Gregory Morse_, Sep 07 2026
